                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "738cc3a1-d4c7-3773-bcab-e77f758b712b",
                        "entry_id": "ed69df05-13ff-3420-abaf-4df98d3a499d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "wat we gewend zijn, niet anders dan het vertrouwde normale"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0c1d31a5-05d4-4ce3-95f7-724981b21c3b",
                                "sense_id": "738cc3a1-d4c7-3773-bcab-e77f758b712b",
                                "text": "Jazzharpist Park Stickney toverde uit dezelfde harp als Van Kesteren een totaal andere klank, met een wat geknepen, jazzgitaarachtige toon. Hoewel zijn frasering en melodische ideeën op piano of gitaar eerder wat gewoontjes zouden zijn, maakte de harp zijn spel bijzonder."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bfd33f8d-c5b0-4cf3-a207-675ccd5182bb",
                        "source_entry_id": "ed69df05-13ff-3420-abaf-4df98d3a499d",
                        "source_sense_id": "738cc3a1-d4c7-3773-bcab-e77f758b712b",
                        "target_lang_word": "commonplace",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "commonplace",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9df96309-3c79-3ed1-9d27-1963fb2b78d1",
                                        "entry_id": "a03146e0-cbbb-3b2b-8044-b471e24121c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ordinary; not having any remarkable characteristics."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45e41af0-5650-45f2-931a-e554ad49469a",
                                                "sense_id": "9df96309-3c79-3ed1-9d27-1963fb2b78d1",
                                                "text": "\"This Mr. Tyrrel,\" she said, in a tone of authoritative decision, \"seems after all a very ordinary sort of person, quite a commonplace man.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91de4b7d-4f20-4b79-b410-ffbb24a381ac",
                                                "sense_id": "9df96309-3c79-3ed1-9d27-1963fb2b78d1",
                                                "text": "In the old days, to my commonplace and unobserving mind, he gave no evidences of genius whatsoever. He never read me any of his manuscripts,[…], and therefore my lack of detection of his promise may in some degree be pardoned."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35f461d7-d6f4-4e20-bcfa-dcc4f6efbd9c",
                                                "sense_id": "9df96309-3c79-3ed1-9d27-1963fb2b78d1",
                                                "text": "I could get hold of nothing but of some commonplace phrases, those futile phrases that give the measure of our impotence before each other's trials."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de6d978a-f5d1-43f2-b613-a6f50069c037",
                                                "sense_id": "9df96309-3c79-3ed1-9d27-1963fb2b78d1",
                                                "text": "In the old days, hopping onto the platform from a not-yet-stopped train was a commonplace stunt for daily commuters in a hurry."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "commonplace",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "08e8aa17-9984-3d87-ad17-9f846a2f9426",
                                        "entry_id": "0adde0f6-3c7d-303a-9bf8-25a58a9d52ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A platitude or cliché."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37216b30-1bc0-4999-8d3f-4fb5942b188d",
                                                "sense_id": "08e8aa17-9984-3d87-ad17-9f846a2f9426",
                                                "text": "Finally he began to mutter some commonplaces which meant nothing particularly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a79c0574-29ad-42f5-b64e-956bf398b07f",
                                                "sense_id": "08e8aa17-9984-3d87-ad17-9f846a2f9426",
                                                "text": "And something angered Tamara in the way the Prince assisted in all this, out-commonplacing her friend in commonplaces with the suavest politeness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "76058551-5556-32a8-9f7f-d23335b50eb2",
                                        "entry_id": "0adde0f6-3c7d-303a-9bf8-25a58a9d52ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something that is ordinary; something commonly done or occurring."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "260ae5b6-8f34-4d93-b309-268f515827c8",
                                                "sense_id": "76058551-5556-32a8-9f7f-d23335b50eb2",
                                                "text": "And, placed discreetly among these commonplaces, a few pieces of genuine quality, bizarrely distinguished by craftsmanship from the vulgar products of the machine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3301203-c0bb-4d0f-a011-7fd199d30022",
                                                "sense_id": "76058551-5556-32a8-9f7f-d23335b50eb2",
                                                "text": "It is odd how easily the common-places of morality or of sentiment glide off in conversation. Well, they are \"exceedingly helpful,\" and so Lord Avonleigh found them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22cb1453-7c6a-4b08-8a82-764d71b3d02f",
                                                "sense_id": "76058551-5556-32a8-9f7f-d23335b50eb2",
                                                "text": "\"MY dear fellow,\" said Sherlock Holmes, as we sat on either side of the fire in his lodgings at Baker-street, \"life is infinitely stranger than anything which the mind of man could invent. We would not dare to conceive the things which are really mere commonplaces of existence.[…]\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de4fa083-da72-40ab-869d-a1d92d2f02f5",
                                                "sense_id": "76058551-5556-32a8-9f7f-d23335b50eb2",
                                                "text": "The smallest commonplace of domestic life, so amiable to the healthy mind, lacerates like a blade."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46aa739b-efd5-44f3-b6f2-651816ce5d46",
                                                "sense_id": "76058551-5556-32a8-9f7f-d23335b50eb2",
                                                "text": "Collecting data via transects is a commonplace in biology[.]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d09647a-2d33-3262-b940-9e1d9dd7502f",
                                        "entry_id": "0adde0f6-3c7d-303a-9bf8-25a58a9d52ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A memorandum; something to be frequently consulted or referred to."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e1a655c-5acd-4b70-bd76-39e35684ca7d",
                                                "sense_id": "7d09647a-2d33-3262-b940-9e1d9dd7502f",
                                                "text": "Whatever, in my reading, occurs concerning this our fellow creature, I do never fail to set it down by way of common-place."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6bcd4012-bf7a-3570-bb7d-f7a7ef16d6a8",
                                        "entry_id": "0adde0f6-3c7d-303a-9bf8-25a58a9d52ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A commonplace book."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "commonplace",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c5680f24-5743-3f03-a8a7-9d3123d4a225",
                                        "entry_id": "5d43bbcd-f0da-36f6-9f38-06c4eda47c32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make a commonplace book."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "06f9ad7b-6e9c-32a9-9d04-df61d6be6dd1",
                                        "entry_id": "5d43bbcd-f0da-36f6-9f38-06c4eda47c32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To enter in a commonplace book, or to reduce to general heads."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87ab9a4d-f267-4859-9799-8b2dd3697c55",
                                                "sense_id": "06f9ad7b-6e9c-32a9-9d04-df61d6be6dd1",
                                                "text": "I do not apprehend any difficulty in collecting and commonplacing an universal history from the […]historians."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "15b274bf-2efd-3652-8d62-b6f1abc12c98",
                                        "entry_id": "5d43bbcd-f0da-36f6-9f38-06c4eda47c32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To utter commonplaces; to indulge in platitudes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd8c6400-0d15-4072-83a5-f232ff95af15",
                                                "sense_id": "15b274bf-2efd-3652-8d62-b6f1abc12c98",
                                                "text": "And something angered Tamara in the way the Prince assisted in all this, out-commonplacing her friend in commonplaces with the suavest politeness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c747928-9cad-48a0-9b7d-ff9e568aa8c2",
                                                "sense_id": "15b274bf-2efd-3652-8d62-b6f1abc12c98",
                                                "text": "c. January 1620, Francis Bacon, letter to the King\nFor the good that comes of particular and select committees and commissions, I need not commonplace."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2b176f19-4e9b-4742-ba79-80fc7cf5142f",
                        "source_entry_id": "ed69df05-13ff-3420-abaf-4df98d3a499d",
                        "source_sense_id": "738cc3a1-d4c7-3773-bcab-e77f758b712b",
                        "target_lang_word": "dismal",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dismal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6c0cc230-2749-3687-9bb7-8a253fd15c20",
                                        "entry_id": "87427bf6-0eeb-3082-b65e-1140e679db96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Disastrous, calamitous."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "20dbc16e-1c8b-3029-8450-c7226c3c0cf7",
                                        "entry_id": "87427bf6-0eeb-3082-b65e-1140e679db96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Disappointingly inadequate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4e72253-80f5-42d6-a768-c2e72a124ff6",
                                                "sense_id": "20dbc16e-1c8b-3029-8450-c7226c3c0cf7",
                                                "text": "He received a dismal compensation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c90f41f-ce7e-4474-8611-41b2daf8050c",
                                                "sense_id": "20dbc16e-1c8b-3029-8450-c7226c3c0cf7",
                                                "text": "Liverpool's efforts thereafter had an air of desperation as their dismal 2012 league form continued."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "469e3344-bb27-3430-bcfc-bf0781cee8ab",
                                        "entry_id": "87427bf6-0eeb-3082-b65e-1140e679db96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Causing despair; gloomy and bleak."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00b704fc-b97e-4afb-9984-1bc861136f16",
                                                "sense_id": "469e3344-bb27-3430-bcfc-bf0781cee8ab",
                                                "text": "The storm made for a dismal weekend"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e28bcab4-36b6-3b13-ae1b-8836377eb748",
                                        "entry_id": "87427bf6-0eeb-3082-b65e-1140e679db96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Depressing, dreary, cheerless."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27ceace2-7b86-493d-ae24-b5a68b21fb1d",
                                                "sense_id": "e28bcab4-36b6-3b13-ae1b-8836377eb748",
                                                "text": "She was lost in dismal thoughts of despair"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ad80dfb-f5df-49bc-b74d-f382bf9a699d",
                                                "sense_id": "e28bcab4-36b6-3b13-ae1b-8836377eb748",
                                                "text": "So, after a spell, he decided to make the best of it and shoved us into the front parlor. 'Twas a dismal sort of place, with hair wreaths, and wax fruit, and tin lambrekins, and land knows what all. It looked like a tomb and smelt pretty nigh as musty and dead-and-gone."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "dismal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6a937de0-e2a6-3fd6-b314-aee0d75a68a7",
                                        "entry_id": "07145a0f-4b21-3307-9f4a-6d9fb9da1a89",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dreary swamp in eastern North Carolina or Virginia in the United States."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "dated",
                                            "possibly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8cc280b0-a5da-423d-bc9b-a0decfb314db",
                                                "sense_id": "6a937de0-e2a6-3fd6-b314-aee0d75a68a7",
                                                "text": ".[…] the proprietors of all the great unimproved tracts of Swamp lands will form themselves into Drainage Companies, by which method alone can we ever hope to witness the complete reclamation of the dismals of the seaboard. No reasonable doubt can be entertained that the clearing and draining of the lands will produce their usual effects in ameliorating the climate and that the tidal portions of No. Caro- lina may thus[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "139b6f40-0f45-4c62-9723-ffafb44f6ff9",
                                                "sense_id": "6a937de0-e2a6-3fd6-b314-aee0d75a68a7",
                                                "text": "The term \"Dismal\" requires some clarification. At one time, all large swamps in eastern North Carolina were commonly referred to as \"dismals,\" probably because they were so gloomy, dreary, and dark, and there are a lot of swamps or \"dismals\" in eastern North Carolina."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0fe99c26-17a7-48d6-8189-dca48e429509",
                        "source_entry_id": "ed69df05-13ff-3420-abaf-4df98d3a499d",
                        "source_sense_id": "738cc3a1-d4c7-3773-bcab-e77f758b712b",
                        "target_lang_word": "trite",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "trite",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ee430a18-b492-3a5d-a835-f8d8b654bc99",
                                        "entry_id": "8d4d6eda-297a-3c3d-9b65-c969d72d35fa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Often in reference to a word or phrase: used so many times that it is commonplace, or no longer interesting or effective; worn out, hackneyed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea0df9b6-b8b2-4c98-a335-0b1c75195715",
                                                "sense_id": "ee430a18-b492-3a5d-a835-f8d8b654bc99",
                                                "text": "It is a trite saying in a young country that anyone starting out in life with the determination to become wealthy will have his wish gratified."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb611f29-6e04-444e-8153-1c1b5a605ea6",
                                                "sense_id": "ee430a18-b492-3a5d-a835-f8d8b654bc99",
                                                "text": "It is trite history – and trite law – to say that the law of the sea since that time [World War II] reflects a history of coastal State expansion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1433dd2c-27b3-4f14-83df-81da3e8778ea",
                                                "sense_id": "ee430a18-b492-3a5d-a835-f8d8b654bc99",
                                                "text": "McPedro the cactus: How to woo a woman! On yehr fahrst date, don’t bring her cut flowers! That’s inhumane! And trite!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a683278-4373-4e39-ba8a-98cc3c0533e2",
                                                "sense_id": "ee430a18-b492-3a5d-a835-f8d8b654bc99",
                                                "text": "This show is sensationally absurd and trite, and if you watch it, you know it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e4c205d8-7300-336d-bf8c-36a4a2473c43",
                                        "entry_id": "8d4d6eda-297a-3c3d-9b65-c969d72d35fa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "So well established as to be beyond debate: trite law."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "227c2b8d-b8b9-413a-b823-253890f486be",
                                                "sense_id": "e4c205d8-7300-336d-bf8c-36a4a2473c43",
                                                "text": "It is trite to say that the mere fact that a decision does not favour the applicant or that the applicant disagrees with the decision does not establish that the decision is tainted with bias."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
